course: dictionary
lesson: 12120
title: Colouration in nature
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Colouration is the pattern and mix of colours on an animal or plant. «The tiger has orange colouration with black stripes.» Here colouration means the whole pattern, not just one colour.
explain: Colouration can also mean the way something is coloured in general, even a slight tint. «The sky had a faint pink colouration at sunset.» The word covers a faint colour as well as a bold pattern.
explain: In science, colouration helps animals survive. Camouflage colouration hides an animal, like a stick insect that looks like a twig. Warning colouration tells predators «I am poisonous», like the bright skin of a poison dart frog.
fact: Colouration is an uncountable noun, so it has no plural: we do not say «colourations».
fact: The US spelling is coloration, without the u.
fact: Camouflage colouration hides an animal, as a stick insect or a snowy owl does.
fact: Warning colouration tells predators «I am poisonous», as a wasp's yellow and black does.
fact: Mimicry is when some animals copy the warning colours of other animals.
exercise: «The poison dart frog has bright colouration.» What does colouration mean here? | The place where the frog lives | The sound the frog makes | *The pattern and mix of colours on the frog | The length of the frog's legs
exercise: Which example shows camouflage colouration? | A bright pink flower | *A stick insect that blends into a twig | A poison dart frog's bright skin | A wasp's yellow and black stripes
exercise: «The sky had a faint pink colouration at sunset.» Which word tells you the colour is only slight? | *faint | colouration | sky | sunset
test: Why do some animals have warning colouration? | To hide from predators | To keep themselves warm | *To tell predators they are poisonous | To make themselves look bigger
test: Which spelling is the US spelling of colouration? | *coloration | colourlation | colouration | colouratoin
exam: Which sentence uses colouration to mean a slight tint? | Mum bought a red coat | *The paper had a faint blue colouration | The frog hid under a leaf | The zebra's stripes are black and white
